# Test Automation Implementation Rule

Only implement automation from an approved TA Story or clearly approved automation scope.

Before coding:
1. identify the TA Story and scenarios being implemented;
2. verify required test data and preconditions exist;
3. verify unresolved blockers do not affect the selected scenarios;
4. inspect the existing repository and reuse established patterns.

## Implementation principles

- Keep tests readable and deterministic.
- Separate test intent from low-level implementation details.
- Reuse existing keywords, fixtures, page objects and API clients where appropriate.
- Do not duplicate helpers unnecessarily.
- Use stable selectors for UI automation.
- Do not use fixed sleeps when a condition-based wait is available.
- Keep test data controlled and non-sensitive.
- Add meaningful assertions for the business outcome.
- Include negative assertions where relevant.
- Do not weaken assertions just to make a test pass.
- Do not change product requirements to fit the automation.

## Before finishing

Report:
- files changed;
- scenarios implemented;
- scenarios not implemented;
- test command used;
- execution result;
- blockers / assumptions;
- requirement-to-test traceability.
